WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 9 Leader Video
Unit 3, Lesson 1: Science

1
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.100
All right, so now we get to talk about science.

2
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.760
We get to talk about design.

3
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.240
We get to talk about DNA.

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.240
We get to talk about, well, let's be honest,

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.840
we get to talk about a lot of things.

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.400
Several of us probably don't have a ton of expertise in.

7
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.800
I mean, we talk about truth and logic

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.040
and even what our faith is.

9
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.480
That's sort of, for most of us youth leaders,

10
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.420
that's in our wheelhouse.

11
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.260
But when we get into things like science,

12
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.140
it gets a little bit more tricky.

13
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.500
You don't have to be an expert in this space.

14
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.180
But I want you to pay attention to a couple of things

15
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.820
and remember a couple of things

16
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.660
as you work through these next several weeks

17
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.620
focusing on things like science.

18
00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.980
Our students are taught.

19
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.220
If you ask your students,

20
00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.100
if you go into the public school classroom

21
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.620
and you look inside of what their textbooks say

22
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.060
and what teachers are saying

23
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.420
is this sort of separation between things of faith

24
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.460
and things of science.

25
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.740
We're told that these things don't belong together.

26
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.100
I remember even back when I was in seventh grade

27
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.540
many years ago, I was told by my teacher

28
00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.140
when I looked up and I saw this chart

29
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.440
of a monkey suddenly becoming more and more

30
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.860
and evolving into a man,

31
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.140
I remember looking at that going,

32
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.740
how can that be?

33
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.620
I remember raising my hand and asking the question,

34
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.540
saying this doesn't seem right.

35
00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.900
And I'll never forget what she said to me.

36
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.820
And it seemed to solve it for me.

37
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.000
And she said, I get what you're saying,

38
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.820
but that is religion and faith.

39
00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.940
And this is science.

40
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.820
Even right there as a seventh grader,

41
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.500
the dichotomy, the split,

42
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.500
the two separate spheres of life were defined for me.

43
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.780
So for our students, that really is what's happening a lot.

44
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.700
And a lot of students are okay

45
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.660
and they're comfortable with that and that's fine.

46
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.500
But the more we research,

47
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.620
the more technologically advanced we become,

48
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.860
the more STEM research and STEM-like subjects

49
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.780
and careers become more popular

50
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.940
and much more pursued by our students post-college,

51
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.860
the more this separation is gonna get defined.

52
00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.620
So it's crucially important that our students understand,

53
00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.740
and guess what?

54
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.260
These two things don't actually need to be separated.

55
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.260
In fact, the more we discover through science,

56
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.060
the more we actually are gonna discover about God,

57
00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.620
the more we discover how awesome he really is.

58
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.180
And over these next couple of weeks,

59
00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.700
you're actually gonna start to see that.

60
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.940
So don't feel like you have to know all the science.

61
00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.380
Don't run out to the library

62
00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.820
and get a bunch of science books

63
00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.500
and try to figure it all out.

64
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.420
I've tried.

65
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.140
Unless that's your thing, knock yourself out.

66
00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:04.780
But for most of us, it's probably not a time thing we have,

67
00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.940
nor maybe even the ability.

68
00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.180
So don't worry about that,

69
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.460
but focus on getting your students to see

70
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.780
that these two worlds actually interconnect.

71
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.540
And I might even suggest

72
00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.140
that find some of those students

73
00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.260
who are really, really like amped up about science

74
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.700
and love it, whether it be math,

75
00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.980
whether it be even computer technology,

76
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.140
anything in the biochemistry,

77
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.580
anything in the science world,

78
00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.180
and get them switched on here and now.

79
00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.020
This is a great way to get some of those students engaged.

80
00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.860
So for this first week,

81
00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.940
I think one of the crucial parts of your gathering

82
00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.900
is gonna be your storyteller.

83
00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.140
Really focus in on somebody

84
00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.420
who can connect science and faith.

85
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.500
So I would suggest either find a university professor,

86
00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.500
find somebody in the science field,

87
00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.420
find somebody who actually does biology or chemistry

88
00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.620
or some field in the sciences

89
00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.900
that is in your church congregation

90
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.860
that can stand and for the students say here,

91
00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:10.580
this is how I connect these two things together.

92
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.780
This is how I can see God

93
00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.220
when I'm looking through a telescope or a microscope.

94
00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:20.460
And this is how I can see God in the field of math

95
00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.220
or whatever it might be.

96
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.780
It's hard.

97
00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.900
And trust me, you're gonna need to sit down

98
00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.420
and probably have a conversation

99
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.940
with the person that you'd like to do this

100
00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.180
and make sure that they can comfortably make that connection.

101
00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.720
I've even talked to Christian educators

102
00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.900
who are math teachers and English teachers

103
00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.260
and science teachers who even as their profession

104
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.180
have a really, really difficult time

105
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.060
sometimes making those connections.

106
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.980
I've done seminars with some teachers

107
00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.380
and helping them to especially math teachers for some reason

108
00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.700
to help them make that connection

109
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.860
so they can see their subject matter

110
00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.740
through a biblical lens.

111
00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.140
So make sure you sit down with those people

112
00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.980
and help them see it if they don't already see it

113
00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.020
but make sure that they can deliver that message

114
00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.540
to your students because this is a crucial moment.

115
00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.780
If your students can see that

116
00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.540
from somebody else in your congregation

117
00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.900
who actually does some of the jobs

118
00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:16.220
that they might be pursuing down the road,

119
00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.860
that's a huge, huge win for you

120
00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.980
as you move forward in this study.

121
00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.700
So in addition to the questions

122
00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.060
that we've provided for you,

123
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.500
it would be a really, really good idea

124
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.820
for you to talk specifically with your students

125
00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.500
about some of the school subjects

126
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.060
and some of the things that they're actually learning

127
00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.060
in school.

128
00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.620
So whatever they happen to be learning

129
00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.780
at this particular time in their curriculum,

130
00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.100
have them talk about that.

131
00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.580
You might even have them bring in their textbooks.

132
00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.260
Have them talk about what are the things

133
00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.460
that they're learning so they can specifically tie in

134
00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:51.620
the subject matter that they're dealing with in school

135
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.060
and their Christian worldview

136
00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.540
so that you can help them make those connections.

137
00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.220
Again, you don't have to know everything

138
00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.900
about that particular subject.

139
00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.500
You guys can work through that together.

140
00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.900
In fact, it's a great opportunity

141
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.700
to have your students teach you

142
00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:04.940
about what they're learning.

143
00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.300
It's gonna help them learn it

144
00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.980
and then you can help them see

145
00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.980
the biblical worldview behind it.

146
00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:14.620
So what we often forget is that in the school world,

147
00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.700
and in a lot of our professional worlds too,

148
00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.940
we have this thing called,

149
00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:23.060
let me just go two different aspects of our world.

150
00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.260
We have what's called the private sphere

151
00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.460
and we have what's called the public sphere.

152
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.380
This is important to get.

153
00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.100
If you think of this as a house,

154
00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:39.220
and this is your upstairs where your bedrooms are

155
00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.580
and what you think and what you do up in your bedrooms

156
00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.420
is your private business, right?

157
00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.380
Not many other people are gonna be up there

158
00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.620
but when you have people over for company or whatever,

159
00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:48.860
you have your public spheres.

160
00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:50.340
This would be your kitchen, your living room

161
00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.780
with those kinds of things.

162
00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.500
These are two different spheres of life

163
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.260
and the things that you do here

164
00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.980
are not the same as what you do here.

165
00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:03.220
Oftentimes, the way we think is the exact same thing.

166
00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.500
So what our students and sometimes us,

167
00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.060
what we'll do is we'll put our school

168
00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.460
or our jobs

169
00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.060
in our public life

170
00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.700
and we'll talk about some things specifically here

171
00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:21.060
but then we'll put our Jesus life up in our private sphere

172
00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.060
and we separate these two things

173
00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.820
and we don't want them to connect

174
00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.500
and we learn to live that way.

175
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.500
Just as I was taught in seventh grade,

176
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.420
this is exactly what my teacher was telling me to do.

177
00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.300
Separate these two things,

178
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.540
live in a two-story home and leave it that way.

179
00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:42.300
What we wanna do is we wanna get rid of this

180
00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.180
and put Jesus down in our public space.

181
00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.020
So here's the bottom line.

182
00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:52.860
Science doesn't actually contradict our faith.

183
00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.020
Instead, it lays a crucial foundation

184
00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.540
for understanding our world.

